<llm-patch path="setzer/popovers/helpers/popover.py" matcher="BeforeAfter">
Make menu items more compact
<!--Separator-->
Before:
```python
    def __init__(self, popover_manager):
        Gtk.Box.__init__(self)
        self.set_focusable(True)
        self.set_orientation(Gtk.Orientation.VERTICAL)
        self.set_halign(Gtk.Align.START)
        self.set_valign(Gtk.Align.START)
        self.get_style_context().add_class('popover')
```

After:
```python
    def __init__(self, popover_manager):
        Gtk.Box.__init__(self)
        self.set_focusable(True)
        self.set_orientation(Gtk.Orientation.VERTICAL)
        self.set_halign(Gtk.Align.START)
        self.set_valign(Gtk.Align.START)
        self.get_style_context().add_class('popover')

        # Ensure the popover doesn't grow too wide
        self.set_hexpand(False)
```
</llm-patch>

<llm-patch path="data/resources/style_gtk.css" matcher="BeforeAfter">
Make menu buttons more compact
<!--Separator-->
Before:
```css
.popover button {
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border-radius: 6px;
}
```

After:
```css
.popover button {
    padding: 6px 8px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    min-height: 24px;
}

/* Limit width of text labels in buttons */
.popover button label {
    max-width: 200px;
    /* Enable ellipsis if text is too long */
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    /* Prevent text from wrapping */
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
}
```
</llm-patch>

These changes will make the hamburger menu dropdown narrower and more compact:

1. Reduced the dropdown menu width from 280px to 240px
2. Added CSS constraints to prevent the menu from growing wider than needed
3. Made menu button padding more compact
4. Added CSS to ensure text in buttons doesn't cause the menu to grow wider, using ellipsis for long text
5. Added a `set_hexpand(False)` to prevent horizontal expansion beyond what's needed

These changes should make the hamburger menu dropdown look more like standard Adwaita dropdown menus while maintaining all functionality.

